        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peachtree_City%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1974 law signed by Governor Jimmy Carter exempted golf carts from vehicle registration, making Peachtree City a pioneer in cart‑friendly streets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peachtree_City%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today the city boasts more than 100 miles of multi‑use paths, a network that grew from that 1974 cart legislation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peachtree_City%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lake McIntosh opened to the public in 2013, adding 650 acres of recreational space to the city’s park system.",
